{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
All you [Bb]peoples come near
Clap [Eb]your hands in [Bb]the air
Shout to God with cries [F]of joy
[Bb]Let the noise ring out [Eb]loud
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The LORD [Bb]Most [F]High is to [Bb]be feared
[Gm]A great King [Eb]over all the [Bb]earth
[Gm]He sub[Eb]dues peoples un[F]der [Gm]us
Na[Eb]tions beneath our [Bb]feet
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He chooses [F]our inher[Bb]i[Bb]tance for us
The pride of Jacob [Eb]whom [Bb]he loves
Selah rests upon the [F]land
[Gm]We stand in [Eb]His command
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
